## Migration Status Report

### ✅ Successfully Implemented 2020-12 Features

#### Core Vocabulary
- [x] `$schema` - dialect identifier
- [x] `$id` - schema identifier  
- [x] `$anchor` - plain-name fragment identifiers (NEW in 2020-12)
- [x] `$dynamicAnchor` - dynamic anchors (NEW in 2020-12)
- [x] `$vocabulary` - meta-schema vocabulary (NEW in 2020-12)
- [x] `$comment` - schema comments
- [x] `$defs` - schema definitions (RENAMED from `definitions`)
- [x] `$ref` - schema references
- [x] `$dynamicRef` - dynamic references (NEW in 2020-12)

#### Array Applicators (Major Changes from draft-07)
- [x] `prefixItems` - tuple validation (REPLACES array form of `items`)
- [x] `items` - now single schema only (CHANGED from draft-07)
- [x] `unevaluatedItems` - unevaluated item validation (NEW in 2020-12)
- [x] `contains` with `minContains`/`maxContains` - enhanced containment

#### Object Applicators
- [x] `properties` - property schemas
- [x] `patternProperties` - pattern-based properties
- [x] `additionalProperties` - additional property schema
- [x] `unevaluatedProperties` - unevaluated property validation (NEW in 2020-12)
- [x] `propertyNames` - property name validation
- [x] `dependentRequired` - required property dependencies (REPLACES `dependencies`)
- [x] `dependentSchemas` - schema dependencies (REPLACES `dependencies`)

#### Validation Keywords
- [x] Number: `minimum`, `maximum`, `exclusiveMinimum`, `exclusiveMaximum` (now numeric), `multipleOf`
- [x] String: `minLength`, `maxLength`, `pattern`, `format`
- [x] String Content: `contentMediaType`, `contentEncoding`, `contentSchema` (NEW in 2020-12)
- [x] Array: `minItems`, `maxItems`, `uniqueItems`
- [x] Object: `minProperties`, `maxProperties`, `required`

#### Type System
- [x] Boolean schemas (`true`/`false`)
- [x] Basic types: `null`, `boolean`, `integer`, `number`, `string`, `array`, `object`

---

### ❌ Missing Critical Features

#### Applicator Keywords (HIGH PRIORITY - BLOCKING)
These are fundamental composition keywords used in virtually all real-world schemas:
- [ ] **`allOf`** - must match ALL of the schemas
- [ ] **`anyOf`** - must match AT LEAST ONE schema
- [ ] **`oneOf`** - must match EXACTLY ONE schema  
- [ ] **`not`** - must NOT match the schema

#### Conditional Keywords (HIGH PRIORITY)
- [ ] **`if`** / **`then`** / **`else`** - conditional validation (from draft-07, kept in 2020-12)

#### Value Constraint Keywords (HIGH PRIORITY)
- [ ] **`enum`** - enumeration of valid values
- [ ] **`const`** - constant value validation (from draft-06)

#### Metadata Keywords (MEDIUM PRIORITY)
- [ ] `title` in `PropertyInstance` (currently only in `SchemaDefinition`)
- [ ] `description` in `PropertyInstance` (currently only in `SchemaDefinition`)
- [ ] `default` - default value
- [ ] `examples` - example values (RENAMED from `example` in draft-06)
- [ ] `deprecated` - deprecation flag (NEW in 2019-09)
- [ ] `readOnly` / `writeOnly` - read/write constraints

#### Validation Implementation (MEDIUM PRIORITY)
The `validate()` method exists but is incomplete:
- [ ] Proper number range validation (min/max/exclusive bounds)
- [ ] String pattern validation (regex matching)
- [ ] String length validation (minLength/maxLength)
- [ ] String format validation (email, uri, date-time, etc.)
- [ ] `allOf`/`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`not` evaluation logic
- [ ] `if`/`then`/`else` conditional logic
- [ ] `enum`/`const` value checking
- [ ] `unevaluatedProperties` actual evaluation logic
- [ ] `unevaluatedItems` actual evaluation logic
- [ ] `dependentRequired` validation
- [ ] `dependentSchemas` validation

#### Reference Resolution (LOW PRIORITY)
- [ ] External reference resolution (HTTP URLs)
- [ ] Circular reference detection and handling
- [ ] Complete `$dynamicRef` evaluation logic
- [ ] Reference caching/optimization

---

### 📋 Recommended Implementation Order

#### Phase 1: Core Applicators (CRITICAL - START HERE)
1. Add `allOf`, `anyOf`, `oneOf`, `not` fields to `SchemaDefinition`
2. Update serde serialization/deserialization
3. Add basic parsing tests
4. Implement validation logic for these applicators
5. Add comprehensive tests

#### Phase 2: Value Constraints (HIGH PRIORITY)
1. Add `enum` keyword (Vec of allowed values)
2. Add `const` keyword (single allowed value)
3. Implement validation logic
4. Add tests for enum/const

#### Phase 3: Conditional Logic (HIGH PRIORITY)
1. Add `if`, `then`, `else` fields to `SchemaDefinition`
2. Implement conditional evaluation in validation
3. Add tests for conditional schemas

#### Phase 4: Complete Validation (MEDIUM PRIORITY)
1. Implement actual validation for number constraints (min/max/exclusive/multipleOf)
2. Implement string pattern matching and format validation
3. Implement `unevaluatedProperties`/`unevaluatedItems` logic
4. Implement `dependentRequired`/`dependentSchemas` validation
5. Improve error messages with detailed paths

#### Phase 5: Metadata & Polish (LOW PRIORITY)
1. Add remaining metadata keywords
2. Add metadata to `PropertyInstance`
3. Improve documentation
4. Add more example schemas

